---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site.config";
// Source: spec/reviewcatcher-legal-pages.md ("Compliance Statement" section).
// Strong draft — for solicitor review before final use; not legal advice.
---

<Layout title={`Compliance | ${siteConfig.name}`} description={`${siteConfig.name} compliance statement.`}>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <h1>Compliance Statement</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: {siteConfig.legal.pagesLastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} is built to keep both us and our clients on the right side of the
        rules. This statement summarises the standards we work to.
      </p>

      <h2>Data protection (GDPR &amp; Irish Data Protection Acts)</h2>
      <p>
        We handle all personal data in line with the EU General Data Protection Regulation and
        the Irish Data Protection Acts. When we process a client's customer data, we do so only
        as a processor, under a signed Data Processing Agreement, strictly on the client's
        instructions.
      </p>

      <h2>Electronic marketing (ePrivacy)</h2>
      <p>
        Messages we send on a client's behalf comply with Ireland's ePrivacy Regulations
        (S.I. 336/2011). We only contact individuals for whom the client has a lawful basis —
        typically existing customers who provided their details and were given the chance to
        opt out — and every message includes a simple opt-out (e.g. reply STOP), which we honour
        immediately.
      </p>

      <h2>Google review guidelines</h2>
      <p>
        Our method complies with Google's review policies. We ask every customer the same way,
        with no incentives and no "gating" (we never filter out unhappy customers or ask only
        happy ones). This keeps our clients' review profiles genuine and within Google's rules.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Personal data is stored in access-controlled systems, encrypted in transit, and reachable
        only by the tools needed to deliver the service. We keep processing records and review
        our providers for appropriate safeguards.
      </p>

      <p>
        Questions or concerns about our compliance can be raised at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>;
        data-protection concerns can also be escalated to the Data Protection Commission
        (dataprotection.ie).
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
